From 5c0d91b031d75e5d7be3de159bd0d70e93b2cc8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ArifiLabs <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:19:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] release: carry the published documents to R86i - NOTICE,
 licences, curated evidence, README, notes, stranger-run DLL step

NOTICE, licenses/ (S-X8 MarlaLabs LICENSE + NOTICE, the libaz cli11/fmt/googletest texts and perfetto's Apache-2.0 text) and the 73 curated r73i receipts under evidence/ are carried unchanged from the r73i publication, which an independent check passed READY. Twelve R86i receipts are added to evidence/ byte-for-byte with their sha256 in MANIFEST.md, and every figure in the README table and in docs/release/RELEASE-NOTES-r86i.md is copied from one of them.

docs/BUILDING.md gains section 4.5: copy the toolchain's runtime DLLs beside the binaries and prove it with a Windows-only PATH. The internal runbook that carried this step is not part of this repository, so a stranger's build had no way to avoid 0xC0000135 / 0xC0000139. Its series replay example now names the real base. OPTIONS-REGISTRY loses one stale duplicate q6_K row, as in r73i.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release documentation for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents, licence texts and receipts only; no code path is touched.
